`asRhoPoly` at the witness point `witPt a b` is a polynomial of `X`-degree `18` in `K[X]`; reducing
it modulo the monic `X ^ 5 - X - C g` yields the explicit remainder `PhiP` (degree `≤ 4`) and
quotient `QP` (degree `13`) recorded here.

* `asN0 … asN4` are the five coefficients of `PhiP` (elements of `K`);
* `asQ0 … asQ13` are the fourteen coefficients of `QP`;
* `asW0 … asW4` are the Bézout multipliers of the certificate `bezout`:
  `∑ asWᵢ · asNᵢ = (a - 3b) ^ 14 · b ^ 10`,
  which shows that `PhiP ≠ 0` whenever `a ≠ 3b` and `b ≠ 0` (note `a ^ 2 - a * b - b ^ 2 =
  (a - 3 * b) ^ 2` in characteristic `5`).

All coefficients are reduced modulo `5`; the corresponding identities are checked by
`ring_nf` + `reduce_mod_char!`.
-/

